*Never*, *never*, *never* stand next to an eel or kraken or other sea
monster that might pull you in, unless you're wearing a non-cursed oilskin
cloak. If you forget, and it still manages to grab you, teleport it away
immediately. You have only one turn to do something; after that you're
dead. Period.

Note that levitation only barely manages to lift you a few centimetres off
the floor or above water: it doesn't protect you from being pulled down
(and out).

